- Emergency Category.
- Brief Case Description.
- Accident Location.
- Time of Incident.
- Time Ambulance Reached Patient.
- Hospital Destination.
- Estimated Arrival Time.

Support two case types:

1. Emergency Case.
2. Normal / Non-Emergency Case.

### Emergency token workflow

After submission:

1. Validate ambulance credentials.
2. Register the emergency case.
3. Generate a unique emergency token.
4. Notify the receiving hospital.
5. Notify the relevant emergency department.
6. Identify available emergency doctors.
7. Check relevant emergency resources.
8. Provide the ambulance with the assigned hospital destination and instructions.
9. Update the hospital dashboard in real time.

Emergency tokens must receive priority over routine OPD queues, subject to authorized clinical triage.

Do not allow automated software to make final clinical severity decisions.

### Emergency dashboard

Display:

- Ambulance ID.
- Patient Information.
- Emergency Token.
- Case Category.
- Assigned Hospital.
- Assigned Department.
- Receiving Doctor / Team.
- Estimated Arrival.
- Emergency Case Status.

Provide a configurable emergency contact and escalation mechanism.

